Provenance of the consent payload templates (spec 016 wave 2, plan risk R-1).

SHAPE ONLY. The owner's question and answer texts are NOT copied; the templates carry __TOKENS__ that the suite fills
with the canonical xprov question of the fixture repository.

Real source (read-only, 2026-10-14): the Claude Code session transcript
  ~/.claude/projects/-Users-rob-claude-projects-noa-planning/ce966712-ed0f-44c3-b401-824ee4468bc1.jsonl
holds an owner-answered AskUserQuestion call. Its tool_use input was
  { questions: [ { question, header, options: [ { label, description } ], multiSelect } ] }
and the result line carried
  toolUseResult = { questions: [...], answers: { "<question text>": "<chosen label>" }, annotations: {} }
  tool_result content (string) = 'Your questions have been answered: "<question>"="<label>". You can now continue with these answers in mind.'
These are the two shapes of post-tool-use.answers.template.json (tool_response = toolUseResult) and
post-tool-use.text.template.json (tool_response = the content string). post-tool-use.none.template.json is the same
envelope with an empty answers map (a question that was dismissed).

NOT measured: what a PostToolUse hook really receives under tool_response, and whether its tool_use_id equals the
PreToolUse one. Plan wave 4 captures one live Pre/Post pair first and replaces these templates if the shape differs.
